       approach (100, 101) and 600 m downstream (103, 104). At lat 40 one
       degree of longitude is about 85.28 km, so 0.003518 deg = 300 m and
       0.003130 deg = 267 m (netconvert gives edge 102 about 305 m once the junction geometry is added).
       The exit link's class (2026-09-25, block 3, WP-83; docs/WEAVE_MODEL_PLAN.md):
       the corridor compiles every off-ramp connection straight (dir="s").
       Way 201 first ran straight from node 4 at +14.4 deg and compiled dir="R"
       (partial right; netconvert: straight below 6 deg), which the EIDM previews
       as a 12 m/s turn. Node 12 now starts it at +4.5 deg for 1.2 m (+4.73 deg
       compiled), then 15.0 deg to node 11 (moved); every compiled lane length
       is unchanged at 0.01 m. -->
